<title>JAPAN: Daiwa Bank problem loans (Banking account).</title>
<headline>Daiwa Bank problem loans (Banking account).</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daiwa Bank Ltd has disclosed</p>
<p>its restructured loans for its banking account (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Sep 96     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans	    282.8	    349.8</p>
<p>  Bad loans			 127.6	    122.3</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	  230.9	    193.1</p>
<p>  Loans to troubled clients   122.6	    141.5</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	   763.9	    806.7</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more. Loans to troubled clients are mainly to the bank's non-bank affiliates.</p>
</text>
